Usage: whereis [OPTION]... NAME...

Locate the binary, source, and manual-page files for each NAME.  By default all categories are searched in the standard locations (PATH for binaries).

OPTIONS:
  -b             search only for binaries
  -m             search only for manual sections
  -s             search only for sources
  -u             search for unusual entries
  -B ARG         define a binary lookup directory
  -M ARG         define a manual lookup directory
  -S ARG         define a source lookup directory
  -f             terminate the last directory list
  -l             list the effective lookup paths
      --help     display this help and exit
  -V, --version  output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
